# CodeSense AI — response headers.
# Baseline security headers apply to EVERY response, including the custom 404
# (an unknown path matches no other block, and the 404 response previously had
# none). Cache rules stay path-specific; Netlify merges them with this block.
# No build step, so asset filenames are not content-hashed: short max-age
# with mandatory revalidation (Netlify ETags make unchanged assets cheap).
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
